<title>AUSTRIA: Lenzing reports 1996 group loss.</title>
<headline>Lenzing reports 1996 group loss.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian fibre maker Lenzing AG said on Thursday it posted a group net loss in 1996 and planned to scrap its dividend.</p>
<p>In a statement, Lenzing reported a net loss of 157.4 million schillings ($13.2 million) after a profit of 253.7 million the previous year. For 1995 it paid a 10 schillings per share dividend.</p>
<p>&quot;1996 was one of the most difficult years in the history of the Lenzing group,&quot; the firm said. ($ = 11.93 Austrian Schillings)</p>
</text>
